{"availability":"available","full":"philipdallen/HuB","name":"HuB","description":"Read-only static dashboard aggregating cross-repo delivery status from four research repositories, with a documented readiness framework and scheduled per-repo automation.","category":"Developer tools","language":"HTML","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-19T20:51:12Z","updated":"2026-10-10T02:38:55Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://philipdallen.github.io/HuB/","topics":["automation","dashboard","github-pages","project-management","research","static-site"],"demo":"https://philipdallen.github.io/HuB/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:22.032Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:22.032Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T07:04:22.032Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T07:04:22.032Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A read-only, static dashboard that aggregates each tracked repo's statuslog.jsonl and renders TRL maturity and Kanban flow metrics per repo. Two files (index.html, config.json) served by GitHub Pages. No build step, no backend, no database.","This is a mirror: it only fetches and displays. Source repos own their own statuslog.jsonl and write it themselves. See HUBAGENTHANDOFF.md for the architecture and its rationale, and PMSTATUSFRAMEWORK.md for the record schema every source repo must match.","index.html is static: no backend, no credentials, and it can only fetch over the public CDN. It cannot call the GitHub API — the unauthenticated budget is 60 requests/hour per visitor IP, and a single page load that fetched comments would spend about a third of it, breaking the page for everyone behind a shared address. So the numbers must be precomputed by a scheduled job, which is automationsweep.yml. It runs with contents: write and writes exactly one file, in this repo. The page stays read-only to visitors."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/philipdallen/HuB/bl